msolveRealSolutions -- compute all real solutions to a zero dimensional system using symbolic methods
*****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        msolveRealSolutions(I)
        msolveRealSolutions(I, K)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, which is zero dimensional, in
        a polynomial ring with coefficients over *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
      * K, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring, or an instance of the type *note
        RingFamily: (Macaulay2Doc)RingFamily,, the field to find answers in,
        which must be one of *note QQi: QQi, (default), *note QQ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, or *note RRi:
        (Macaulay2Doc)RRi, (possibly with specified precision)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Threads => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 5, number
        of processor threads to use;
      * Verbosity => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0,
        level of verbosity between 0, 1, and 2;
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of lists; each entry in the list
        consists of a list representing the coordinates of a solution. By
        default each solution coordinate value is also represented by a *note
